course: dictionary
lesson: 11671
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning is right. The word «assets» is a good example. Money words, people words and game words each point to a different meaning.
explain: «The family's assets include a house and their savings.» Here assets are things you own that are worth money. In money lessons, debts are what you owe, so assets and debts are often talked about together.
explain: «Maya is a great asset to the team.» Here an asset is a useful person or quality. «The game needs new assets, like pictures and sounds.» Here assets are files used in a game or app.
fact: Assets is a noun, and its singular form is asset.
fact: In money, assets are things a person or company owns that are worth money, like a house, savings or machines.
fact: An asset can also be a useful quality, skill or person, as in «a great asset».
fact: In computing, assets are files like pictures and sounds that are used in a game or app.
fact: Useful phrases to know: «a great asset» and «assets and debts».
exercise: «The family's assets include a house and their savings.» What are assets in this sentence? | *Things a person owns that are worth money | Sounds and pictures used in a game | A kind and helpful friend | Things a person owes to other people
exercise: «Maya is a great asset to the team.» What does asset mean here? | *A useful person or quality | Money a company owes | Something that is bad for the team | A type of machine
exercise: «The game needs new assets, like pictures and sounds.» What are assets in this sentence? | Savings in a bank | Rules for the game | *Files used in a game or app | Clothes for the players
test: «Her skill at maths is an asset to our class.» What does asset mean here? | A debt | *A useful quality | A type of game | A loud noise
test: Which phrase means the things you own and the things you owe? | Savings and pictures | Assets and games | *Assets and debts | A great asset
exam: «Our new computer is a real asset to the school.» What does asset mean here? | Money the school owns | *A useful thing or quality | Game files on the computer | A debt the school must pay
